                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "All participants must strictly follow the Audax Club Parisien (ACP) randonneuring regulations. This is a non-competitive brevet: it is a challenge against the distance and clock, not other riders. Mandatory safety equipment includes a certified helmet worn at all times, functional permanently attached front white/rear red lights, and a high-vis reflective vest/sash worn during dark hours. No support vehicles are allowed between controls.\n\nIn case of severe mechanical or physical issues resulting in a DNF (Did Not Finish), please report it immediately to the ride host.\n\nOrganizer Contact: Aliaksandr R. (+375 17 955-4218 / info@rbelby.cc)",
